WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.625
Catalyst, reimagined, is a student portal redesign by Aayush Keshari, Nipun Chandra, and Shivam Kharangate.

00:00:05.625 --> 00:00:10.500
This guided walkthrough uses captured states from the working prototype, with synthetic narration.

00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:14.625
The focus is finding classes and knowing when enrollment is complete.

00:00:14.625 --> 00:00:17.626
Every student record and registration action is fictional.

00:00:17.626 --> 00:00:23.251
The dashboard brings the next semester, academic essentials, and a current schedule into one workspace.

00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:27.188
The classes workspace connects discovery and registration.

00:00:27.188 --> 00:00:32.950
A student can search by course code, title, or instructor, including a code with spaces.

00:00:32.950 --> 00:00:36.792
Common filters cover subjects, open seats, format, and meeting days.

00:00:36.792 --> 00:00:40.633
Each section shows its instructor, meeting time, location, and availability.

00:00:40.633 --> 00:00:47.932
Search context stays with the selected student and semester, so returning to the search does not mean starting over.

00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:53.047
A comparison view makes section differences visible without navigating away.

00:00:53.047 --> 00:00:58.014
Here, two User Interface Design sections meet on different days and at different times.

00:00:58.014 --> 00:01:01.207
The comparison also shows credits, seats, instructor, and prerequisites.

00:01:01.207 --> 00:01:03.690
Students can compare up to three sections.

00:01:03.690 --> 00:01:06.883
Adding a selection to the cart is explicitly planning.

00:01:06.883 --> 00:01:10.076
It does not reserve a seat or complete enrollment.

00:01:11.500 --> 00:01:16.877
In this captured review, Senior Design section one and UI Design section one overlap.

00:01:16.877 --> 00:01:22.638
The prototype names the conflicting class and explains how to recover by choosing another section.

00:01:22.638 --> 00:01:25.711
Confirmation is disabled, and no classes are enrolled.

00:01:25.711 --> 00:01:32.241
The same validation layer checks prerequisites, registration status, duplicate courses, seat availability, holds, and the credit limit.

00:01:32.241 --> 00:01:35.698
Replacing UI Design with section two resolves this conflict.

00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:41.769
Once the selection is valid, the student reviews and confirms the complete enrollment.

00:01:41.769 --> 00:01:45.438
A receipt records the semester, time, course sections, and credits.

00:01:45.438 --> 00:01:49.106
This is the explicit transition from planning to confirmed enrollment.

00:01:49.106 --> 00:01:50.574
The schedule updates immediately.

00:01:50.574 --> 00:01:53.142
A failed review leaves the selection unchanged.

00:01:53.142 --> 00:01:56.444
Waitlisting remains a separate status and never implies enrollment.

00:01:56.444 --> 00:02:00.112
Dropping a confirmed class requires confirmation and offers immediate undo.

00:02:01.500 --> 00:02:05.611
Academic progress separates earned credits from current coursework and future registration.

00:02:05.611 --> 00:02:14.582
The senior sample profile has ninety six earned credits, fifteen in progress, and fifteen remaining after this term, assuming those current courses are passed.

00:02:14.582 --> 00:02:20.562
The student can review a synthetic transcript, use a graduation checklist, and download a readable summary.

00:02:20.562 --> 00:02:23.926
An advisor must confirm actual requirements and final eligibility.

00:02:25.500 --> 00:02:30.770
On a narrow screen, the schedule becomes an agenda with meeting details still available.

00:02:30.770 --> 00:02:36.418
Academic services groups support destinations, while tasks and preferences stay local to each demo profile.

00:02:36.418 --> 00:02:41.312
The case study explains the source review, background research, design decisions, and implementation.

00:02:41.312 --> 00:02:43.194
Twenty one behavioral tests pass.

00:02:43.194 --> 00:02:49.218
Real student feedback is still needed, and no participant results or measured usability improvements are invented.

00:02:49.218 --> 00:02:52.606
Explore the working prototype to try the complete workflow.

